course: dictionary
lesson: 6715
title: Offer: giving, deals and watching out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Offer can be a doing word (a verb) or a naming word (a noun). As a verb, to offer means to say you will give something, or to hold it out for someone to take. «Offer to help» means you say you are willing to help. The words around offer give you clues about which meaning fits.
explain: As a noun, an offer is a deal, like a lower price: a special offer. It can also mean the money or thing someone says they will give. When you meet offer, ask yourself: is someone giving something, or is there a deal on the table?
explain: Context also helps you spot an offer that is not safe. «Countdown timers on offers are there to rush you, so you buy before you think.» The clue is rush. A good offer does not need you to hurry, so if you feel pushed, stop, and check with a trusted adult.
fact: To offer means to say you will give something, or to hold it out for someone to take.
fact: To offer to do something means you say you are willing to do it.
fact: An offer is a deal, such as a special offer or a lower price.
fact: In maths, work out the real cost per item: «buy 2, get 1 free» may or may not be a good deal.
fact: Be careful of offers that seem too good to be true: «Zara's online friend offered a gift card if she told him her address.» Never share your address with someone online.
exercise: «To join a game, stand close, watch, offer to help, then ask to play.» What does offer to help mean here? | You hand over the game to someone else | *You say you are willing to help | You refuse to help | You are paid to play
exercise: «Dad's shop has a special offer: buy 2, get 1 free.» What kind of offer is this? | *A deal that can save you money | A rude reply | A loud noise in the street | A type of shoe
exercise: «You may be offered slippers, TAPochky, when you visit a flat.» What does offered mean here? | *Given or held out to you | Taken away from you | Sold to you at a high price | Dropped on the floor
test: «Zara's online friend offered a gift card if she told him her address.» What is the safest answer to a stranger's offer like this? | *Say no, and tell a trusted adult | Give your address at once | Send your password too | Share it with all your friends
test: «Countdown timers on offers are there to rush you.» What does rush suggest about the offer? | *You may be pushed to buy before you think | You will get a prize for free | It means to run fast to the shop | The offer is always fair
exam: In «I can offer you a seat», is offer a verb or a noun? | adverb | adjective | noun | *verb
